<td id="A1.T5.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.4pt;padding-right:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T5.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Iteration 2 and 6 of Stage 2</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Experimental configurations for OOD and ID settings.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We observed that the extended 40-iteration search in Stage 2 was consistently beneficial for scenarios involving more than 50 adapters, justifying our setup for the large-scale OOD task.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Algorithm flow of Evo-Merging</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We summarize the procedure of <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Evo-Merging</span> in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix B Algorithm flow of Evo-Merging ‣ Black-box Model Merging for Language-Model-as-a-Service with Massive Model Repositories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Evo-Merging Procedure</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
           Collection of LoRa pairs <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{i},B_{i}\}_{i=1..N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{i},B_{i}\}_{i=1..N}</annotation></semantics></math>, validation data <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}}</annotation></semantics></math>, regularization parameters <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
           Merged LoRa pair <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{A}_{m},\mathcal{B}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{A}_{m},\mathcal{B}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
           
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
           <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Sparsity-Based Denoising</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
           Set uniform weights <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\leftarrow 1/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\leftarrow 1/N</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1..N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1..N</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
           <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{pm}}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{i}\cdot B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>pm</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{pm}}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{i}\cdot B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
           Use CMA-ES to find optimal <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}^{*}\leftarrow\underset{\bm{\alpha}\in[0,1]^{N}}{\text{argmin}}\Big(\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathcal{M}(A_{\text{pm}}(\bm{\alpha}),B_{\text{pm}}),\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>argmin</mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝜶</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>pm</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>pm</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}^{*}\leftarrow\underset{\bm{\alpha}\in[0,1]^{N}}{\text{argmin}}\Big(\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathcal{M}(A_{\text{pm}}(\bm{\alpha}),B_{\text{pm}}),\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
                   <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}+\lambda_{1}||\bm{\alpha}||_{1}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝜶</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}+\lambda_{1}||\bm{\alpha}||_{1}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            where <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{pm}}(\bm{\alpha})=\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{i}\cdot\mathbf{S}_{\alpha_{i}}(A_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>pm</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{pm}}(\bm{\alpha})=\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{i}\cdot\mathbf{S}_{\alpha_{i}}(A_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
           
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
           <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Sign-Aware Scaling</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
           Create sparsified LoRa-A matrices:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
           <span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{S}_{\alpha_{i}^{*}}(A_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐒</mi><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{S}_{\alpha_{i}^{*}}(A_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
           <span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
           Use CMA-ES to find optimal <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\beta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\beta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\beta}^{*}\leftarrow\underset{\bm{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}}{\text{argmin}}\Big(\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathcal{M}(\bm{\beta}),\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>argmin</mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝜷</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ℝ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜷</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\beta}^{*}\leftarrow\underset{\bm{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}}{\text{argmin}}\Big(\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\mathcal{M}(\bm{\beta}),\mathcal{D}_{\text{val}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
                  <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}+\lambda_{2}||\bm{\beta}||_{1}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝜷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}+\lambda_{2}||\bm{\beta}||_{1}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            where <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(\bm{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜷</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(\bm{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math> uses <math id="alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{m}=\sum\beta_{i}A^{\prime}_{i},\mathcal{B}_{m}=\sum\beta_{i}B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{m}=\sum\beta_{i}A^{\prime}_{i},\mathcal{B}_{m}=\sum\beta_{i}B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
           
</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
           <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Construct Final Merged Model</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
           <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{m}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta_{i}^{*}\cdot A^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{m}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta_{i}^{*}\cdot A^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
           <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{m}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta_{i}^{*}\cdot B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{m}\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta_{i}^{*}\cdot B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Details of Baselines</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides a detailed description of the baseline methods used for comparison in our experiments. Each method is summarized by its core concept and a simplified mathematical representation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A3.I1" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Individual Model</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each task utilizes an independently fine-tuned model, serving as an upper-bound for single-task performance. The model for a specific task <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task Arithmetic <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ilharco et al. 2023b</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Merges models by arithmetically combining their “task vectors” (<math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), which represent the difference between fine-tuned (<math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) and pre-trained (<math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{pre}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{pre}}</annotation></semantics></math>) weights.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{m}=\theta_{\text{pre}}+\lambda\sum_{t}\tau_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{m}=\theta_{\text{pre}}+\lambda\sum_{t}\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TIES-Merging <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yadav et al. 2023</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Resolves interference by a three-step process: <span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">T</span>rimming low-magnitude parameters, <span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E</span>lecting a dominant sign, and <span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">S</span>eparately merging parameter groups that agree on the sign.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{m}=\text{TIES}(\{\tau_{t}\})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>TIES</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{m}=\text{TIES}(\{\tau_{t}\})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DARE (Drop and Rescale) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al. 2024b</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sparsifies task vectors by randomly <span id="A3.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>ropping a high proportion (<math id="A3.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>) of delta parameters (<math id="A3.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>) and <span id="A3.I1.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RE</span>scaling the survivors by <math id="A3.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math> to preserve the original model’s embeddings.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\frac{\delta\odot(1-m)}{1-p},\quad\text{where }m\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\frac{\delta\odot(1-m)}{1-p},\quad\text{where }m\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DELLA-Merging <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deep, Bhardwaj, and Poria 2024</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Employs a novel pruning technique, MAGPRUNE, which samples delta parameters for dropping based on their magnitude, followed by sign election and fusion.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\text{drop}_{i})\propto 1/|\delta_{i}|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>drop</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\text{drop}_{i})\propto 1/|\delta_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EMR-Merging <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. 2024b</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Creates a unified model by <span id="A3.I1.ix6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E</span>lecting a shared parameter base, then generates lightweight task-specific <span id="A3.I1.ix6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">M</span>asks (<math id="A3.I1.ix6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <span id="A3.I1.ix6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R</span>escalers (<math id="A3.I1.ix6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) to align the direction and magnitude for each task.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}_{t}=\lambda_{t}\cdot(M_{t}\odot\theta_{\text{unified}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>unified</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}_{t}=\lambda_{t}\cdot(M_{t}\odot\theta_{\text{unified}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix7" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Breadcrumbs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Davari and Belilovsky 2024</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Constructs multi-task models by creating a sparse ’breadcrumb’ mask (<math id="A3.I1.ix7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) that filters out both low-magnitude and high-magnitude outlier weights from task vectors on a layer-wise basis.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{m}=\theta_{\text{pre}}+\alpha\sum_{t}(m_{t}\odot\tau_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{m}=\theta_{\text{pre}}+\alpha\sum_{t}(m_{t}\odot\tau_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix8" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LoRaHub  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. 2024a</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Achieves cross-task generalization by dynamically composing a set of pre-trained LoRA modules (<math id="A3.I1.ix8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) for a new task using a gradient-free optimization to find the optimal combination weights (<math id="A3.I1.ix8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{composed}}=\sum_{i}w_{i}m_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>composed</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{composed}}=\sum_{i}w_{i}m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix9" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LoRa (Low-Rank Adaptation) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. 2021</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adapts pre-trained models by freezing the original weights (<math id="A3.I1.ix9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) and injecting trainable low-rank decomposition matrices (<math id="A3.I1.ix9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.ix9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>) into each layer.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\leftarrow W_{0}+BA" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\leftarrow W_{0}+BA</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix10" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(IA)<sup id="A3.I1.ix10.1.1" class="ltx_sup">3</sup> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2022</a>)</cite></span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Injects and learns minimal scaling vectors (<math id="A3.I1.ix10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>) that modulate internal activations (<math id="A3.I1.ix10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>), allowing for efficient adaptation with extremely few trainable parameters.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}=l\odot h" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}=l\odot h</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A3.I1.ix11" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.ix11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best Adapter</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A3.I1.ix11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A non-compositional baseline that selects the single best-performing source adapter (<math id="A3.I1.ix11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) on the target task’s validation set (<math id="A3.I1.ix11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{val}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}=\arg\min_{m_{i}}\mathcal{L}(m_{i},D_{\text{val}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}=\arg\min_{m_{i}}\mathcal{L}(m_{i},D_{\text{val}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Dataset Details and Metric</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Dataset</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments in this paper are conducted using the <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InstructUIE</span> benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2023</a>)</cite>, a large-scale, unified framework for Information Extraction (IE). The core innovation of InstructUIE is its reformulation of diverse IE tasks into a single, generative text-to-text format. This unification is the key technical enabler that allows us to represent specialist models, each trained on fundamentally different extraction objectives, within a comparable parameter space, making them viable candidates for merging.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our experimental methodology hinges on the creation of a large and deeply heterogeneous <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">source model pool</span>. We fine-tuned over 100 specialist <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama 3.1 Instruct</span> models, where each model was trained to master one of the specific, granular IE tasks defined by InstructUIE. To provide the reader with a clear understanding of what exactly is being merged in our framework, we detail the hierarchy of these tasks below.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The Hierarchy of Information Extraction Tasks</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The tasks within InstructUIE represent different layers of semantic understanding, from identifying simple entities to deconstructing complex events. Our model pool contains specialists for each of the following task categories:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer 1: Named Entity Recognition (NER) — The Foundational Layer.</span> This is the most fundamental IE task, focused on locating and classifying atomic pieces of information—the ”who,” ”what,” and ”where” in a text.</p>
<ul id="A4.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Primary Task: Named Entity Recognition (NER).</span> This is the complete task: to both identify an entity’s text span and assign it a type (e.g., identifying ”Apple Inc.” and labeling it as ‘Organization‘).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Auxiliary Task: Entity Span Extraction (ES).</span> A simpler, decomposed version of NER that only focuses on identifying the boundaries of an entity (e.g., finding ”Apple Inc.”) without knowing its type.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Auxiliary Task: Entity Typing (ET).</span> The other half of the NER problem: given a specific text span like ”Apple Inc.”, the task is to assign the correct label (‘Organization‘).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer 2: Relation Extraction (RE) — Connecting the Dots.</span> Building upon the foundation of entities, RE focuses on identifying the semantic relationships that connect them.</p>
<ul id="A4.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Primary Task: Relation Extraction (RE).</span> The complete task of identifying a full semantic triplet, including two entities and the relation between them (e.g., ‘(Steve Jobs, founded, Apple Inc.)‘).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Auxiliary Task: Entity Pair Identification (EP).</span> A simpler task that only identifies that a pair of entities is related, without specifying the nature of the relationship (e.g., identifying that ‘(Steve Jobs, Apple Inc.)‘ is a related pair).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Auxiliary Task: Entity Pair Relationship Identification (EPR).</span> The classification component: given a pair of entities ‘(Steve Jobs, Apple Inc.)‘, the task is to classify the relationship as ‘founded‘.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer 3: Event Extraction (EE) — Deconstructing Structured Scenarios.</span> This is the most complex layer, focused on extracting information about dynamic occurrences or events, including who did what to whom, when, and where.</p>
<ul id="A4.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Primary Task: Event Extraction (EE).</span> The complete task of identifying an event, its type, its trigger word, and all its associated arguments with their specific roles (e.g., for a ‘Purchase‘ event, identifying the ‘Buyer‘, ‘Seller‘, and ‘Item‘).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Auxiliary Task: Event Trigger Identification (EET).</span> The first step in EE: identifying the key word or phrase that triggers the event (e.g., the word ”bought”) and classifying the event’s type (‘Purchase‘).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Auxiliary Task: Event Argument Extraction (EEA).</span> The second step: given an event trigger and its type, the task is to find all the entities participating in that event and assign them their correct roles (e.g., identifying ‘Google‘ as the ‘Buyer‘ and ‘YouTube‘ as the ‘Item‘).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, our source pool of 100+ models is populated with specialists from <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">all nine of these distinct tasks</span>. The core challenge for our <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Evo-Merging</span> framework, particularly in the Out-of-Domain setting, is therefore to intelligently fuse knowledge from this highly diverse collection. It must learn how to leverage the foundational knowledge of an <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ES</span> model, the relational logic of an <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EPR</span> model, and the structural understanding of an <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EEA</span> model to generalize effectively to a new, unseen task.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Datasets</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluations are conducted in two settings. The <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-domain</span> evaluation assesses multi-task capability by merging and testing on eight NER datasets: ACE_2005 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Walker et al. 2006</a>)</cite>, CrossNER_AI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2020</a>)</cite>, CrossNER_Lit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2020</a>)</cite>, FabNER <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar and Starly 2021</a>)</cite>, Mit-Movie, MultiNERD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tedeschi and Navigli 2022</a>)</cite>, TweetNER <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ushio et al. 2022</a>)</cite>, and WikiANN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan et al. 2017</a>)</cite>. The <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">out-of-domain</span> evaluation, our core test for zero-shot generalization, uses six datasets that are entirely unseen by the source model pool. These include two datasets for NER (<span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MIT Restaurant Review</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2019</a>)</cite> and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FindVehicle</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guan 2022</a>)</cite>), two for RE (<span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NYT</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Riedel, Yao, and McCallum 2010</a>)</cite> and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CoNLL2004</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roth and tau Yih 2004</a>)</cite>), and two for Event Trigger (ET) identification (<span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mit-Movie</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2019</a>)</cite> and <span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FabNER</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar and Starly 2021</a>)</cite>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate all models using Macro-averaged F1-score and Precision. These metrics are standard for information extraction, effectively handling the typical class imbalance of the task. Precision measures the reliability of LLM’s generation.The F1-score provides a single, balanced measure of overall performance. We report the macro-average, which computes the metric per instance before averaging, to ensure every sample contributes equally to the final score.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluation follows a strict matching criterion, where entities, relations, or triggers are correct only if all their components (e.g., span and type) exactly match the ground truth. To ensure a fair and robust comparison, this process is normalized:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case-Insensitive:</span> All text is converted to lowercase before comparison, preventing capitalization differences from affecting scores.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Order-Insensitive:</span> The set of extracted items is treated as unordered, meaning the generation order does not influence the result.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Pre-selection Strategy for Baselines in OOD Setting</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The large(over 100), noisy model pool in the out-of-domain (OOD) setting poses a significant challenge for most baseline methods, leading to performance degradation and making hyperparameter tuning infeasible.We implemented the following two-stage pre-selection protocol exclusively for these baselines:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A5.I1" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A5.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adapter Pre-selection:</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each target OOD task, we first identified a promising subset of source adapters (typically less than 10) based on their generalization performance on the same validation set. This step filters for the most relevant models. The resulting curated adapter sets used for each task are detailed in Table <a href="#A5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix E Pre-selection Strategy for Baselines in OOD Setting ‣ Black-box Model Merging for Language-Model-as-a-Service with Massive Model Repositories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A5.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter Tuning:</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A5.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On these manageable subsets, we then performed an extensive grid search to find the optimal hyperparameters for each baseline (e.g., density and <math id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>). The best-performing configurations, which were used in our main results, are summarized in Table <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Hyperparameter Grid Search for Baseline Methods ‣ Black-box Model Merging for Language-Model-as-a-Service with Massive Model Repositories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In stark contrast, this pre-processing pipeline was not applied to our <span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Evo-Merging</span> framework or LoRaHub. Both were benchmarked directly on the entire pool of 100+ models, rigorously testing their inherent robustness and ability to navigate noisy, large-scale fusion scenarios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T6.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T6.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="A5.T6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;" colspan="3"><span id="A5.T6.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TIES-Merging</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;" colspan="3"><span id="A5.T6.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DARE</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;" colspan="3"><span id="A5.T6.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Della</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;" colspan="3"><span id="A5.T6.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Breadcrumbs</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T6.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T6.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="A5.T6.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Params (<math id="A5.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda,p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda,p</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="A5.T6.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prec.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="A5.T6.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">F1</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="A5.T6.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Params (<math id="A5.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda,p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda,p</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="A5.T6.1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prec.</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="A5.T6.1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">F1</span></td>
<td id="A5.T6.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="A5.T6.1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Params (<math id="A5.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda,p,\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda,p,\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
